@karya0 Can we avoid the changes to `base.py` and `spec.py`?

From Claude:
The load-bearing fix is entirely inside kvcr/: hold the buffer export (ctypes.c_char.from_buffer(primary_kv_view), currently discarded at manager.py:353) in a module-level list for as long as NIXL has the registration — a module global, not an instance field, so it also survives the KeyboardInterrupt path where no handler runs and the munmap comes from GC. That needs no changes to base.py, tiering/base.py or tiering/spec.py; optionally add a BufferError branch to SharedOffloadRegion.cleanup() that keeps mmap_obj, unlinks the /dev/shm path and logs, so the retention is explicit rather than resting on an invisible export chain.

